_ddg_taint_reaches gates on fn_has_ddg = source_fn in ddg_symbols, where
source_fn is the ANALYZER's symbol id. The python LanguageDdgSpec supplied
neither name_for nor kind_for, so _walk_functions fell back to the bare `name`
field and the constant kind "function", and every method was stored under a key
nothing ever constructs. Measured before: 0 of 24,915 methods matched, while
21,257 of them (85.3%) WERE in the set under the unreachable bare-name
spelling. 68.5% of python callables could never have fn_has_ddg true, so every
taint finding rooted in one was structural BY CONSTRUCTION.

py.py's naming rule was DERIVED from the analyzer, not assumed. A probe over all
four shapes gives top / top.inner / Outer.meth / Inner.deep -- prefix with the
IMMEDIATE enclosing scope, one level, class or function; kind is "method"
exactly when that scope is a class. Nested FUNCTIONS were mis-keyed too, which
the row had not noticed.

